             :kind :function
             :intent "(my.test/run-owned {:seon.ns/name 'my.e1probe}) from MCP agent e1-probe (hosted on :agent-665a30c12282) refused three times on default fb1437312 (2026-09-28, 2.2-5.1 s, 325k-435k armed calls each): no branch or commit <fresh checkpoint head> to branch from (:seon.cluster.registry/source-absent, request branch :agent-...). The same prepare-checkpoint! -> open-overlay! -> branch! sequence by hand from the default instance's store succeeds in 840 ms. The agent branch's world base is the stale adopted commit 6abadd62 while the cluster records 6abae0f5, so each request prepares a new checkpoint and retires the other checkpoint-default-* ones. Every such run also carried a diagnostic: seon.turn.batch/join-write refused its own output contract (:seon.batch/join). No agent on its own branch can prove a task, so no fault it fixes ever closes. Done when that run answers the test's red result and a regression runs a named test from a hosted agent branch."
